(6711483, 1002090, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier, coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>My first reaction, "Holy smokes - that is some demolition dust being kicked up". But then on closer inspection it is not dust - it''s MOTION! This is a really cool long exposure shot. People rushing to their destinations, flowing down the stairs. They seem to burst into dust at the bottom of the escalator in the flurry of their activity. The escalator can be seen as a representation of life and life''s journey.  The end of the destination at the bottom of the escalator is where it comes to an end and where all life returns to dust/ash.</td>', 'Voted earlier, coming back to comment. My first reaction, "Holy smokes - that is some demolition dust being kicked up". But then on closer inspection it is not dust - it''s MOTION! This is a really cool long exposure shot. People rushing to their destinations, flowing down the stairs. They seem to burst into dust at the bottom of the escalator in the flurry of their activity. The escalator can be seen as a representation of life and life''s journey.  The end of the destination at the bottom of the escalator is where it comes to an end and where all life returns to dust/ash.', '2012-03-15 14:50:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6711485, 1004527, 10785, '<td valign="top">Cropping about 60-70% of the background out would have helped a lot!</td>', 'Cropping about 60-70% of the background out would have helped a lot!', '2012-03-15 14:56:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6711490, 1004490, 10785, '<td valign="top">Very cool cross processing and you captured a neat little spurt of movement with the girl at an interesting angle of view. The scene is somewhat cluttered so a focal point is lacking (Other than the one created by the moving girl...) and there is no link to Christmas Day in the picture. For all I know this could have been Independence Day or Memorial Day or Labor Day in Suburban America...</td>', 'Very cool cross processing and you captured a neat little spurt of movement with the girl at an interesting angle of view. The scene is somewhat cluttered so a focal point is lacking (Other than the one created by the moving girl...) and there is no link to Christmas Day in the picture. For all I know this could have been Independence Day or Memorial Day or Labor Day in Suburban America...', '2012-03-15 15:08:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6711548, 1004415, 68956, '<td valign="top">Creepily wonderful :)</td>', 'Creepily wonderful :)', '2012-03-15 17:01:33.000000', NULL, 1),
